message: "Please cite the software version or commit used for reproduction."
type: software
title: "Binary-memory retention and maintenance heat: reproducibility software"
authors:
  - family-names: "Salih"
    given-names: "Mahgoub A."
    affiliation: "Department of Physics, College of Science, Qassim University, Saudi Arabia"
abstract: >-
  Numerical verification of two-codeword binary-memory retention and ideal
  correction heat, including contraction bounds, posterior conditional entropy,
  biased logical marginals and binomial-tail asymptotics. The exact lifetime
  optimum is restricted to uniform logical marginals and ideal control.
keywords:
  - "information thermodynamics"
  - "memory retention"
  - "binary symmetric channel"
  - "Landauer principle"

version: "2026.10.04"
date-released: 2026-10-04
